		{
			dependencies: ["0C4E18B05F9E68DE"]
			description: [
				"&6Surface Mounted Devices&r, or &6SMD&rs for short, are &2more efficient ways to produce the Circuit components you've been making.&r"
				""
				"All SMD components must be produced in at least a &2HV Assembler&r, and they all will require liquid &9Polyethylene&r."
				""
				"Start off with the &6SMD Transistor&r. These are simply a &6Gallium &2Foil&r and &6Fine Annealed Copper Wire&r."
				""
				"Next up are &6SMD Resistors&r, which are also simple: &6Carbon Dust&r and &6Fine Electrum Wire&r."
				""
				"Next up are &6SMD Diodes&r, which are fairly simple. &2Gallium Arsenide Dust&r and &6Fine Platinum Wire&r net you half a stack.&r"
				""
				"Then are &6SMD Capacitors&r. You'll need sheets of &6Polyvinyl Chloride&r to make these, or they can also be made more slowly with &6Silicone Rubber&r. &2Using Tantalum Foil in place of Aluminium doubles your yield."
				""
				"Finally, &6SMD Inductors&r. Made with &6Nickel Zinc Ferrite&r and &6Fine Cupronickel Wire.&r"
				""
				"Invest in a robust system of automation for SMD components and all of their ingredients, since you'll need them in large quantities for several tiers to come. They will also work in place of the non-SMD versions you've been using in all but the simplest of recipes."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: false
			id: "7256E0064F967C93"
			rewards: [{
				count: 3
				id: "568615DC956F2D3C"
