		{
			dependencies: [
				"5B07A88C0BFF6586"
				"4F572CA3678CB287"
			]
			description: [
				"Now that you have your &3Microverse Projector&r, you will need to project a microverse for the &6microminers&r to use. This is done using &6Universe Creation Data&r and quite a bit of &6Quantum Flux&r."
				""
				"Looking at the Creation Data's uses in &bEMI&r, you'll see that it changes the microverse type to Normal. For quite a while, all microminers will require the Normal microverse type to run."
				""
				"After projecting your microverse, the inside of the projector will change appearance, and you should be ready to send off your first microverse mission."
			]
			id: "7ACF867DECE1C37F"
			tasks: [{
				id: "42587449855B384F"
				item: "kubejs:universe_creation_data"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Projecting Microverses"
			x: 28.75d
			y: 5.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["281C7940CD437B69"]
			description: [
				"If you wish to create an off-Earth base or otherwise conduct operations longer than a mining trip, &3Ad Astra&r offers a few machines that will be helpful or even necessary to your objective."
				""
				"1. The &3Oxygen Distributor&r. When supplied with &aRedstone Flux (RF)&r and &9Oxygen&r, this machine creates a breathable volume of air around it which expands to fit the environment it's contained in up to six thousand (6000) blocks in volume. It also prevents &9Water&r in this area from freezing, and is therefore necessary for the operation of a &3Rock Crusher&r."
				""
				"2. The &3Oxygen Sensor&r. This block emits a redstone signal and displays a green light when it's in an oxygenated environment. Check one before you take your helmet off to ensure you don't suffocate!"
				""
				"3. The &3Gravity Normalizer&r. This machine unlocks in &5EV&r, and when supplied with &aRF&r it allows you to control gravity nearby similar to the Oxygen Distributor. If the low gravity on &bThe Moon&r or in &bOrbit&r bothers you, then give it a whirl!"
			]
			icon: "ad_astra:space_painting"
			id: "4288A253129B1E75"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "590467B0584D0075"
					item: "ad_astra:oxygen_distributor"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "01DCC71F3DEA223F"
					item: "ad_astra:oxygen_sensor"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "5AFCEFEA48FF7835"
					item: "ad_astra:gravity_normalizer"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "An Extraterrestrial Abode"
			x: 28.75d
			y: 4.25d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&n&9Monifactory&r&r shares an official Discord server with the other projects under Omicron Industries, which serves as a useful community resource."
				""
				"On the server, there are flowcharts and guides to help you with many parts of the pack accessible via the server's helpful bot, development announcements and more are available in the &n#announcements&r channel, and the community helps with tech support questions, and investigates possible bug reports."
				""
				"You can also chat with many fellow players there if you like, who are largely willing to help with general questions one might have."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"[\"\",{\"text\":\"To join the server, you can use the button on the Main Menu to go to the join URL, or if you're not into Discord you can find other projects from Omicron Industries, on \"},{\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"text\":\"this\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://github.com/Omicron-Industries\"}},{\"text\":\" GitHub page.\"}]"
				""
				"[\"\",{\"text\":\"Issue tracking and development is handled on the respective GitHub project repositories. The repository for this pack is \"},{\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"text\":\"here\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://github.com/Omicron-Industries/Monifactory\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
			]
